      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i'm stuck on this stripe integration. i keep getting a 402 error back in the json response even though i'm using a test card that should work. what are the usual reasons for a 402 and how should i check if my request payload is actually the problem?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A 402 error with Stripe, especially when using test cards, usually indicates a problem with the payment method itself or the authorization process, not necessarily that your code is entirely wrong. It can sometimes mean the card was declined for a reason Stripe can't detail in the test environment, or there might be an issue with how you're passing the token or payment details. To check your payload, you should meticulously compare your request structure against Stripe's official documentation for the specific API endpoint you are hitting. Look closely at required fields, data types, and ensure any necessary metadata or customer IDs are present.",
